# Example HTTP requests for Visual Studio / JetBrains HTTP client / compatible REST clients.
# Update the port to match the URL shown by IIS Express.
# Run these only against a disposable local database.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:26536

### List products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Shop
Accept: application/json

### Create product (implementation uses PUT, not POST)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Shop
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "ProductName": "Desk lamp",
  "ProductDescription": "Warm white LED",
  "ProductPrice": 499.00
}

### Update product — replace Product_ID with a real existing ID
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Shop
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Product_ID": 1,
  "ProductName": "Desk lamp",
  "ProductDescription": "Updated LED model",
  "ProductPrice": 549.00
}

### Invalid name should produce HTTP 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Shop
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "ProductName": "No",
  "ProductDescription": "Invalid short product name",
  "ProductPrice": 10
}

### Delete product — replace 1 with a disposable local product ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Shop?productID=1
Accept: application/json
